---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FAQ from '../../components/FAQ.astro';
import GuideArticle from '../../components/v2/templates/GuideArticle.astro';
import { siteImages } from '../../data/images';
import { getPageSEO } from '../../utils/seo';

const faqItems = [
  { question: 'What should I do first in Karinderya?', answer: 'Follow the current tutorial prompts and learn one complete customer-service cycle before changing several restaurant systems.' },
  { question: 'Which Wiki section should a new player open first?', answer: 'Start with the Guides Hub, then use Recipes, Ingredients, Equipment, Workers, and Furniture when those topics appear during play.' },
  { question: 'Where can I find ingredient information?', answer: 'Use the Ingredients Hub for individual entries and the Recipes page for the wider cooking workflow.' },
];
const pageSEO = getPageSEO('guides-beginner-guide');
const relatedLinks = [
  { label: 'Guides Hub', href: '/guides/', description: 'Browse every player guide by topic.' },
  { label: 'Recipes', href: '/recipes/', description: 'Learn how Recipes connect ingredients, cooking, and food.' },
  { label: 'Equipment', href: '/equipment/', description: 'Browse cooking equipment and restaurant tools.' },
  { label: 'Basic Stove', href: '/equipment/basic-stove/', description: 'Open the individual Wiki entry for this Stove.' },
  { label: 'Workers', href: '/workers/', description: 'Review Worker management and related guidance.' },
  { label: 'Furniture', href: '/furniture/', description: 'Explore Tables, Chairs, and layout planning.' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  pageId="guides-beginner-guide"
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Guides', href: '/guides/' }, { label: pageSEO.h1 }]}
>
  <GuideArticle
    title={pageSEO.h1}
    kicker="Getting started guide"
    intro="Follow the current tutorial, learn one order-to-service cycle, and use the Wiki when a specific system needs more explanation."
    tableOfContents
    heroImage={siteImages.beginnerGuideHero}
    relatedLinks={relatedLinks}
  >
    <h2 id="direct-answer">First Steps</h2>
    <p>Start with the tutorial shown by the current game. Learn how the interface presents a customer request, cooking task, completed food, and service interaction before expanding into optional systems.</p>

  <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
  <p>Public gameplay supports a basic order, kitchen, and serving loop. The exact recipe inputs, Worker behavior, restock timing, rating rules, and equipment differences should be confirmed from their focused pages rather than assumed during the first session.</p>

  <h2 id="how-it-works">How It Works</h2>
  <p>A restaurant task usually begins with customer information and moves toward preparation and service. Read what the game currently shows, keep the active task easy to identify, and complete the workflow before taking on more work than you can follow.</p>

  <h2 id="first-service-process">First Service Process</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Follow the tutorial and interface prompts shown by the current game.</li>
    <li>Identify the customer and read the current order information.</li>
    <li>Review the ingredients and kitchen equipment connected with preparation.</li>
    <li>Keep the active cooking task easy to identify.</li>
    <li>Return to the dining area and complete service.</li>
    <li>Repeat the workflow and note which Wiki category you want to explore next.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="using-the-wiki">Using the Wiki</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Food and Recipes:</strong> understand the cooking and serving relationship.</li>
    <li><strong>Ingredients and Grocery:</strong> review materials used by the restaurant workflow.</li>
    <li><strong>Equipment:</strong> browse the Stove directory and the current limited Chiller entry.</li>
    <li><strong>Workers:</strong> review the system and its version-sensitive hiring guide.</li>
    <li><strong>Furniture:</strong> plan Tables, Chairs, and dining-area layout.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="gameplay-tips">Gameplay Tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Learn one complete service cycle before handling several tasks.</li>
    <li>Keep the kitchen and dining route easy to follow.</li>
    <li>Review ingredient information before beginning preparation.</li>
    <li>Change one part of restaurant organization at a time.</li>
    <li>Use the <a href="/guides/co-op-guide/">Co-op Guide</a> when playing with teammates.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="common-mistakes">Common Mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Skipping current tutorial or interface instructions.</li>
    <li>Starting preparation before reading the active order.</li>
    <li>Changing several restaurant areas before learning the basic workflow.</li>
    <li>Focusing on customization while work areas remain unclear.</li>
  </ul>

    <FAQ slot="faq" items={faqItems} />
  </GuideArticle>
</BaseLayout>
